          %h3#indexed_category_of_a_functor Indexed category of a functor
          %p Combining these previous examples we get
          #CartesianFunctorIndexing.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}
              a functor and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^* \mathbb{C}
              given by
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mo *
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi I
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F^* \mathbb{C})^I = \mathcal{C}/F(I)
                \.
            %p
              If the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} \to F^* \mathbb{C}
              of
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %h3#indexed_category_of_a_topos_over_a_base_topos Indexed category of a topos over a base topos
          %p
            This situation frequently arises when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \coloneqq f^*
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            part of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f
                  \:
                  \\mathcal{C}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}}
                  \\mathcal{S}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this way, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            is a topos, then to be thought of as a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            %em over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            (i.e. an object of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+2-category"} slice 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} /S
            %em relative to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            for more on this.
          %p
            Also, via this indexed category,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
            (see there) over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+topology"} canonical topology
          %h3#hyperdoctrine Hyperdoctrine
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
          %h3#indexed_monoidal_category Indexed monoidal category
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+category"} indexed monoidal category
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+closed+monoidal+category"} indexed closed monoidal category
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
          %h3#indexed_category
            Indexed
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 1)
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+%28infinity%2C+1%29-category"} indexed (infinity, 1)-category
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#extensions_of_adjunctions_to_indexed_categories Extensions of adjunctions to indexed categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R) :
                    \\mathcal{C} \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} \mathcal{S}
            %p
              be a pair of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+categories"} finitely complete categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              extends to an
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R} : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{S}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
              is the self-indexing of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CanonicalSelfIndexing"}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is the base change indexing of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianFunctorIndexing"}
            %p
              By the general properties of adjunctions on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategories"} overcategories
              (see there) we get for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in \mathcal{S}
              an adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi I
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L/I \dashv R/I) : \mathbb{C}^I = \mathcal{C}/R(I) \to \mathcal{S}/I = \mathbb{S}^I
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} : I \mapsto R/I
              is always a
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L} : I \mapsto L/I
              is if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianFunctorIndexing"}
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{L} \dashv \mathbb{R}) :
                    \\mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{S}
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, lemma B1.2.3
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p (…)
          %h3#WellPoweredness Well-powered indexed categories
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is called
              %strong well-powered
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \mathbb{C} \to \mathcal{S}
              corresponding to it under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              has the property that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Rect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U : Q(2, \tilde \mathbb{C})
                    \\to
                    Rect(*,\tilde \mathbb{C})
            %p
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(2,\tilde \mathbb{C})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rect(2, \tilde \mathbb{C})
              on vertical
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, example. B1.3.14
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : \mathcal{C} \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} \mathcal{S}
              be a pair of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves pullbacks. Then the
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is well powered if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
              is.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, prop. B1.3.17
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+functor"} indexed functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+topos"} indexed topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+Grothendieck+construction"} indexed Grothendieck construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+category"} indexed monoidal category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"}> internal category
                ,
                %span.newWikiWord
                  externalisation
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/externalisation"} ?
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of
            %em indexed categories
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Grothendieck60
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              , §A.1 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1958-1960__5__299_0.pdf#page=3"}> p. 3
              ) of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Technique de descente et théorèmes d’existence en géométrie algébrique. I. Généralités. Descente par morphismes fidèlement plats
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+Bourbaki"} N. Bourbaki
              exp. no190 (1960) 299-327 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1958-1960__5__299_0"}> numdam:SB_1958-1960__5__299_0
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            but under the name “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"}> fibered category
            ” (
            %em> catégorie fibrée
            ) which later became the standard term, instead, for the (
            %a{:href => "Grothendieck+construction#EquivalenceBetweenFiberedCategoriesAndPsuedofunctors"}> equivalent
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            on an indexed category, cf.:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Bénabou1975"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              , p. 898 (2 of 41) of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fibrations petites et localement petites
              %strong 281
              Série A (1975) 897-900 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k6228235m/f171.image#"}> gallica
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p An early monograph:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.+T.+Johnstone"}> P. T. Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+Par%C3%A9"} R. Paré
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+D.+Rosebrugh"} R. D. Rosebrugh
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Schumacher"} D. Schumacher
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+J.+Wood"} R. J. Wood
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+C.+Wraith"} G. C. Wraith
              = succeed "," do
                %em Indexed Categories and Their Applications
              %strong 661
              (1978) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0061360"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0061360
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Early discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
